Hostbay's design follows patterns from uniterm (https://github.com/ys-ll/uniterm),
Copyright its contributors, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
Any file that includes code copied or adapted from uniterm names it in a header
comment and keeps uniterm's copyright notice.

The terminal colour themes (src/theme/terminalThemes.ts), the .itermcolors reader
(src/theme/itermcolors.ts) and the translations in src/i18n/ (zh-CN, zh-TW, ja,
ko, de, es, fr, ru, pt and vi) are taken from uniterm, Copyright 2025 uniTerm,
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. Hostbay renamed uniterm's own two
terminal themes and kept only the translations whose English matches Hostbay's.
The terminal themes reproduce published colour schemes by their authors:
Solarized (Ethan Schoonover), Monokai (Wimer Hazenberg), Dracula (Zeno Rocha and
the Dracula Theme contributors), Molokai (Tomas Restrepo), Tomorrow (Chris
Kempson), One Dark and One Light (the Atom project), GitHub (GitHub, Inc.),
Gotham (Andrea Leopardi), Hybrid (Andrew Wong), Nord (Arctic Ice Studio and
Sven Greb), Gruvbox (Pavel Pertsev), Catppuccin (the Catppuccin organization),
Tokyo Night (enkia), Rosé Pine (the Rosé Pine organization) and Everforest
(sainnhe).

